id: pmc-52px
title: "Single-window generation ignores an item release field, retro-dating already-shipped work"
description: "Duplicate check: searched all statuses for release field attribution shipped-in retro-date closed_at window pin single-window; existing pmc-vl87/pmc-ew5n cover item REFERENCE rendering only, and no item covers release attribution in the single-window path. pm-changelog places an item from itemTimestamp() = closed_at ?? updated_at ?? created_at. The multi-window path (--all-release-tags / assignItemsToReleaseWindows) additionally PINS an item into the window whose tag matches the item release field regardless of timestamps, but the single-window path used by every fleet repo changelog / changelog:check / release:notes script ignores the release field entirely. Consequence: a tracker whose fix shipped in release X but whose item is closed later lands in the CURRENT release window, so the changelog claims months-old work as new, and the two generation paths disagree about the same item."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: changelog,correctness,multi-agent,release-attribution
created_at: "2026-07-24T19:26:27.775Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T20:26:53.446Z"
deadline: "2026-07-25T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-24T20:26:53.445Z"
author: claude-opus-5
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Single-window generation honors an item release field (top-level or metadata) under an opt-in flag; An item pinned to a release other than the window version is excluded from that window; An item pinned to the window version is included regardless of its timestamp; Default output stays byte-identical when the flag is absent; --explain reports items excluded by release attribution
why_now: Multi-agent workflows routinely ship a PR in one release and close the tracker in a later one; without release attribution the changelog is wrong and agents are forced to leave trackers open forever (3 such items across the fleet today).
resolution: "Added the opt-in --respect-item-release flag (SDK respectItemRelease) so a declared release field pins an item to its window in single-window generation, mirroring what assignItemsToReleaseWindows already did for --all-release-tags. usesSingleVersionSection() mirrors buildSections() branching so grouped and history paths are untouched. --explain reports the new stage and exclusions."
expected_result: "A tracker closed long after its fix shipped can be attributed to the release that shipped it, so closing it no longer injects months-old work into the current release window."
actual_result: "Verified with real pm data across the standalone CLI, pm changelog generate, pm changelog export, --all-release-tags and --explain; dogfooded on pmc-sall (attributed to 2026.6.13 and closed, filed under its own release heading). Default output is byte-identical — proven against all 17 sibling repos' own changelog args. 174/174 tests green."
component: generator
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind}:
