comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T19:26:27.775Z",claude-opus-5,"Root cause of the fleet-wide shipped-but-unclosed tracker backlog (pmc-sall, pm-csv-69ln, pm-slack-gx2h): closing them today would inject their entries into the current release window."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T19:26:27.775Z",claude-opus-5,"Reproduced with real data in a throwaway pm workspace: item with release=2026.6.1 closed 2026-07-24 renders under 2026.6.1 via --all-release-tags but under 2026.7.24 via --release-version 2026.7.24 --since 2026-07-24T00:00:00Z."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T19:26:27.775Z",claude-opus-5,Any time-window report keyed on closed_at silently misattributes work when the tracker is closed after the release that shipped it; an explicit release field is the only durable attribution signal.
